          "title": "You'll want to know: صحو",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "صحو — ṣaḥw — \"clear weather; cloudless\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "الطقس صحو اليوم. aṭ-ṭaqs ṣaḥw al-yawm. The weather is clear today."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "صحو (ṣaḥw) is built on the native Arabic root ṣ-ḥ-w, \"to be cloudless\" (Lane). Lane gives it of a day when the clouds have gone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
